  levelTitle: Bridge Defender - Four Diode Rectifier
  initialPage: 0
  pages:
  - title: LEVEL 26 | Bridge Defender | Four Diodes
    explanation: 'A bridge rectifier uses four diodes to keep the load polarity consistent.
      The DC-input teaching solution follows: battery positive -> switch -> D1 anode
      -> D1 cathode -> R1 -> green LED -> D4 anode -> D4 cathode -> battery negative.
      D2 and D3 are reverse-biased and block. The visual layout is illustrative,
      not live solver output.'
    caption: PAGE 1/4 | 5 V | FOUR 1N4007 | 220 OHM | GREEN LED
    parts:
    - id: battery
      kind: 0
      position: {x: 0.09, y: 0.48}
      label: 5 V
      color: {r: 0.98, g: 0.29, b: 0.35, a: 1}
    - id: sw1
      kind: 5
      position: {x: 0.25, y: 0.76}
      label: SW1
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.78, b: 0.28, a: 1}
    - id: d1
      kind: 3
      position: {x: 0.43, y: 0.84}
      label: D1 A >| K  ON
      color: {r: 0.3, g: 0.98, b: 0.59, a: 1}
    - id: d2
