  - title: LEVEL 26 | Which Diodes Conduct?
    explanation: 'Normal polarity: input A=SwitchOutput is positive with respect
      to input B=Battery_negative. D1 runs from A to bridge output P; D4 returns
      from bridge output N to B. D2 runs from B to P and D3 runs from N to A, so
      both block. With a reversed DC input, the conducting pair swaps. This level
      evaluates only normal input polarity; do not reverse the battery in gameplay
      unless the level supports it.'
    caption: PAGE 3/4 | D1 + D4 ON | D2 + D3 OFF
    parts:
    - id: battery
      kind: 0
      position: {x: 0.09, y: 0.48}
